// Ch10 B08 side scene (optional): "Why do they swim?" (E, 3 min, ~150 words). act2_ch10.md §4. A Kirru
// child (about twenty: a child, already taller than Rhen) climbs out of the water beside Asha. Curious,
// not wise. Asha starts the Order's answer and can't finish it. No Kirru adult intervenes.
title: ch10_why_swim
location: ch10/reedhollow
---
@camera R06
@mark kirru_child platform_edge_child walk
@anim kirru_child look_at asha_staff
@wait 2.5
Kirru_child as "Kirru child" [neutral]: You are the one who makes the dead swim. #line:ch10_swim_001
Asha [sad]: I led them out to sea. At Corrow. #line:ch10_swim_002
Kirru_child as "Kirru child" [neutral]: Why do they swim? Ours go up. #line:ch10_swim_003
Asha [worried]: They go to rest in the sea, until the— #line:ch10_swim_004
@wait 2.0
-> I don't know. #line:ch10_swim_005
    <<set $ch10_asha_answered_child = true>>
    Kirru_child as "Kirru child" [neutral]: Then ask them. #line:ch10_swim_006
-> Because we're afraid to let them go. #line:ch10_swim_007
    <<set $ch10_asha_answered_child = true>>
    @wait 1.5
    Kirru_child as "Kirru child" [neutral]: Yes. You-people hold everything. #line:ch10_swim_008
@mark kirru_child lagoon_swim walk
@wait 2.0
@mark rhen platform_edge_rhen walk
@wait 1.5
Asha [sad]: I didn't finish the sentence, Rhen. I've said it all my life. #line:ch10_swim_009
<<set $ch10_child_asked = true>>
===
